## 2. Recommended Technology Stack

### Desktop Runtime

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| **Desktop shell** | **Tauri v2** (Rust) | Tiny binary (~3 MB vs 150+ MB Electron), native OS APIs, filesystem access, system tray, auto-update, security sandboxing. Embeds the Next.js frontend as a webview. |
| **IPC** | Tauri IPC (invoke commands) | Type-safe bridge between frontend TS and backend Rust. Zero-copy where possible. |

### Backend Core

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| **Primary language** | **Rust** | Memory safety, zero-cost abstractions, excellent async (tokio), native filesystem perf, compiles to single binary. |
| **API server** | **Axum** (Rust) | Lightweight, async, tower-based. Serves REST + WebSocket for real-time progress/streaming. |
| **Task orchestration** | **Tokio** tasks + channels | Async scanning, indexing, and AI inference run as background tasks with progress reporting. |
| **Python sidecar** | **Python 3.11+** (optional) | Only for specific AI tasks where Python-exclusive libraries are needed (e.g., advanced document parsing). Bundled as a sidecar process. |

### Storage

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| **Relational DB** | **SQLite** (via `rusqlite` / `sea-orm`) | Zero-config, embedded, single-file, ACID. Stores all metadata, permissions, settings, file records, relationships, knowledge graph edges. |
| **Vector DB** | **Qdrant** (embedded mode) | Runs in-process via Rust bindings. No separate server needed. HNSW indexing, filtering, payload storage. Handles semantic search vectors. |
| **Full-text search** | **Tantivy** (Rust) | Rust-native Lucene equivalent. BM25 ranking, tokenization, stemming. Sub-millisecond keyword search over tens of thousands of documents. |

### AI / ML

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| **Local LLM** | **Ollama** | Simple local model server. Supports Llama 3.1, Mistral, Phi-3, Gemma 2, etc. REST API. User can choose model size based on hardware. |
| **Embedding model** | **all-MiniLM-L6-v2** or **nomic-embed-text** via Ollama | Runs locally. 384-dim vectors. Fast inference on CPU. Good semantic quality. |
| **Vision / OCR** | **LLaVA** or **Moondream** via Ollama | Local image understanding. Describes images, reads text in screenshots, understands diagrams. |
| **Document parsing** | **pdf-extract**, **docx-rs**, **calamine** (Rust crates) | Native Rust parsers for PDF, DOCX, XLSX. No Python dependency for core parsing. |
| **Cloud LLM (optional)** | **Gemini API** / **OpenAI API** | For users who opt-in to cloud AI for higher quality responses. Always opt-in, never default. |

