## 5. Search Architecture

### Hybrid Search Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Q["User Query"] --> A["Query Analyzer"]
    A --> B["Intent Classifier"]
    
    B -->|"Keyword Match"| C["Tantivy BM25"]
    B -->|"Semantic"| D["Qdrant Vector Search"]
    B -->|"Both"| C
    B -->|"Both"| D
    
    C --> E["Result Merger (RRF)"]
    D --> E
    
    E --> F["Re-ranker"]
    F --> G["Filter & Boost"]
    G --> H["Final Results"]
    
    A --> I["Extract Filters"]
    I -->|"category, date, project"| G
```

### Search Modes

| Mode | Engine | Example |
|------|--------|---------|
| **Keyword** | Tantivy | `"main.py"`, `"README"` |
| **Semantic** | Qdrant | `"projects using machine learning"` |
| **Hybrid** | Both + RRF fusion | `"smart farmer AI project"` |
| **Natural Language** | LLM → structured query → Hybrid | `"find my AWS certificate from last month"` |
| **Image** | Vision model description → Qdrant | `"photos where I'm presenting"` |
| **Code** | AST-aware Tantivy + Qdrant | `"functions that handle authentication"` |

### Ranking Strategy

1. **Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)**: Combines BM25 and vector scores
2. **Recency boost**: Recently modified files score higher
3. **Category boost**: Match file category to query intent
4. **Project affinity**: Files in active projects score higher
5. **Relationship boost**: Files connected in the knowledge graph get bonus

