## 7. File Indexing Strategy

### Discovery Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    A["Permission Granted Folders"] --> B["Recursive Directory Walker"]
    B --> C{"Should Index?"}
    C -->|"Yes"| D["Compute Content Hash"]
    C -->|"Skip"| E["Add to Exclusion List"]
    
    D --> F{"Already Indexed? Hash Match?"}
    F -->|"New/Changed"| G["Extract Content"]
    F -->|"Unchanged"| H["Skip"]
    
    G --> I["Classify File Type"]
    I --> J["Parse & Chunk"]
    J --> K["Generate Embeddings"]
    K --> L["Store in Qdrant"]
    J --> M["Index in Tantivy"]
    J --> N["Store Metadata in SQLite"]
    
    G --> O["AI Summarize (background)"]
    O --> N
```

### Exclusion Rules (Default)

```
node_modules/
.git/objects/
__pycache__/
.venv/
dist/
build/
.next/
*.lock
*.log
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.map
*.wasm
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
```

### Incremental Indexing

1. **Initial scan**: Full recursive scan on first setup (~2-5 minutes for a typical workspace)
2. **File watcher**: Use `notify` (Rust crate) for real-time filesystem change detection
3. **Content hashing**: SHA-256 hash to detect actual content changes vs. timestamp-only changes
4. **Delta updates**: Only re-index changed files, update vectors and search index incrementally
5. **Background processing**: AI summarization and relationship detection run as low-priority background tasks

### Project Detection Heuristics

A directory is classified as a "project" if it contains any of:

| Indicator | Confidence |
|-----------|-----------|
| `package.json` | High |
| `requirements.txt` / `setup.py` / `pyproject.toml` | High |
| `Cargo.toml` | High |
| `.git/` directory | High |
| `pom.xml` / `build.gradle` | High |
| `Makefile` + source files | Medium |
| `README.md` + structured subdirectories | Medium |
| `*.sln` / `*.csproj` | High |
| `go.mod` | High |
| `Dockerfile` | Medium |

