## 8. Vector Database Strategy

### Why Qdrant (Embedded)

| Criteria | Qdrant | ChromaDB | Milvus | FAISS |
|----------|--------|----------|--------|-------|
| **Embedded mode** | ✅ Rust native | ❌ Python server | ❌ Distributed only | ✅ Library |
| **Filtering** | ✅ Rich payloads | ⚠️ Basic | ✅ Rich | ❌ None |
| **Performance** | ✅ HNSW + quantization | ⚠️ Moderate | ✅ Fast | ✅ Very fast |
| **Persistence** | ✅ On-disk | ✅ On-disk | ✅ On-disk | ❌ In-memory |
| **Rust integration** | ✅ Native client | ❌ Python only | ❌ gRPC | ⚠️ C++ FFI |
| **Production ready** | ✅ | ⚠️ | ✅ | ⚠️ |

### Configuration

- **Distance metric**: Cosine similarity
- **Index type**: HNSW with product quantization for memory efficiency
- **Dimensions**: 384 (matching `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` or `nomic-embed-text`)
- **On-disk storage**: `~/.neurodesk/qdrant/`
- **Expected scale**: 50K-500K vectors for a typical power-user workspace

