## 9. Security & Privacy Model

### Core Principles

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Privacy is the #1 feature.** Every architectural decision must default to local-only processing.

### Privacy Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph "Always Local"
        A["File Scanning"]
        B["Content Indexing"]
        C["Vector Embeddings"]
        D["Full-text Search"]
        E["Knowledge Graph"]
        F["Metadata Storage"]
    end
    
    subgraph "User Opt-in Only"
        G["Cloud LLM Queries"]
        H["Google Account"]
        I["GitHub Integration"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Never"
        J["Automatic File Upload"]
        K["Telemetry with File Content"]
        L["Third-party Analytics on User Data"]
    end
```

### Security Measures

| Area | Implementation |
|------|---------------|
| **File access** | Explicit folder permission grants only. Stored in SQLite. Revocable anytime. |
| **Data at rest** | SQLite with optional SQLCipher encryption. Qdrant data in user-owned directory. |
| **API keys** | Stored in OS-native credential store (`windows-credentials` / `keychain`). Never in plaintext config. |
| **Cloud AI** | User must explicitly enable. Each query shows what context is sent. Toggle per-conversation. |
| **Auto-update** | Tauri's built-in updater with code signing verification. |
| **Process isolation** | Tauri's security model: frontend cannot directly access filesystem. All access through Rust commands. |
| **Exclusion list** | Users can mark files/folders as "never index" from the UI. Respected globally. |

### Data Residency

All data stored under `~/.neurodesk/`:

```
~/.neurodesk/
├── db/
│   └── neurodesk.db          # SQLite (metadata, settings, graph)
├── qdrant/                    # Vector database files
├── tantivy/                   # Full-text search index
├── cache/
│   ├── thumbnails/            # Generated file previews
│   └── summaries/             # Cached AI summaries
├── config.toml                # Non-sensitive settings
└── logs/
    └── neurodesk.log          # Rotated application logs
```

